
# Walkthrough: Deep Research Agent (Phase 3)

> **Date:** 2026-01-11
> **Status:** ✅ Completed
> **Target:** `mcp-server-nucleus`

## 🎯 Goal
Activate the **Deep Research Agent** by enabling real web search (DuckDuckGo) and page reading (BeautifulSoup) capabilities.
This replaces the previous "Simulation Mode" with actual internet access.

## 🛠 Changes Implemented

### 1. WebOps Upgrade ([web_ops.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/capabilities/web_ops.py))
- **Search**: Integrated `duckduckgo-search` (v4+) for real query results.
- **Reading**: Integrated `beautifulsoup4` for clean text extraction from HTML.
- **Dependencies**: Added to [pyproject.toml](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/pyproject.toml) and verified in `.venv`.

### 2. Researcher Persona ([.brain/agents/researcher.md](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/7c654df4-b83e-43f9-8620-f15868ec39d1/.brain/agents/researcher.md))
- Created a **Deep Research Protocol**.
- Defined the "Looping" strategy:
  1. Plan Query.
  2. Search & Select.
  3. Read & Extract.
  4. Synthesize & Cite.

## ✅ Verification
- **Test Script**: [tests/test_researcher.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tests/test_researcher.py) (Passed).
- **Execution**:
  - `web_search("python 3.12 features")` -> Returned real StackOverflow/Python.org links.
  - `web_read_page("python.org")` -> Extracted "Welcome to Python.org".

## 🚀 How to use
```bash
nucleus spawn "Research the latest breaking changes in Next.js 15"
```
The agent will now actually browse the web to answer.
